infinity_v3 -- INFOIL 1.0 Adoption Notice

Licensor: Infinity Core Contributors. This is a collective description of the
individual copyright holders and their authorized licensors, identified by
applicable source notices and contribution records. It is not a separate
legal entity, an assignment of copyright, or a claim that any contributor
owns or may relicense another contributor's work. Each grants only rights
that they own or are authorized to license.

License: Infinity Optimized Inference License, INFOIL 1.0.
Effective date: 2026-10-12.
First covered source release: infinity_v3-infoil-1.0 (Git tag).
Pre-adoption base: 9486dd9ee89575442fda1a491c381046b37e116e.

Covered material and rights:
INFOIL is the license offered for original fork contributions and
copyrightable fork modifications first distributed under this adoption,
and later contributions intentionally submitted and accepted on that basis,
in this repository's application, shared libraries, build tools, and
documentation. It is also the offered license for those contributors'
rights in the derivative distribution as a whole. The included INFOIL text
sets the conditions for those rights; the scope and exclusions in this
notice govern which material and independently held rights it covers.

Excluded material and independent grants:
Inherited Hugging Face Text Embeddings Inference code retains Apache-2.0.
Previously Apache-licensed fork contributions retain their existing grants.
Bundled and external third-party components retain their own licenses and
attribution, including separately licensed Candle extensions and native
vendor code. Model weights, datasets, and dependencies do not become
INFOIL-covered merely through use or inclusion. See NOTICE,
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, and retained file-level and component notices.

This adoption does not revoke earlier grants, even for previously published
source without a public binary or container release. Someone relying on an
independent Apache or other grant for the material it covers may continue
to exercise that grant. It does not confer rights to later INFOIL-only
contributions. Retained upstream notices identify the inherited material;
new covered fork modifications must carry notices identifying the change
and referring to this adoption scope.

INFOIL is source-available with provider and infrastructure restrictions,
including private, single-customer endpoints and GPU-hour billing. It is
not an unrestricted open-source license. Baseten deployments are expressly
permitted under INFOIL Section 4. This exception does not make Baseten the
Licensor or copyright owner of others' contributions.

The complete INFOIL terms and retained original Apache license follow so
this file can accompany standalone packages and native installations.
Separate copies are in LICENSES/INFOIL-1.0.txt and
LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt. LICENSING.md explains the adoption and examples.

